---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { meta } from '../../data/snapshot';
---
<Base
  title="Data Terms · CCIR"
  ogImage="/og/documents.png"
  description="Terms governing use of CCIR's published series and data — viewing, quotation and citation with attribution, and the permission requirement for systematic retrieval or redistribution."
  showTape={false}
>
  <section class="wrap top">
    <header class="page-head">
      <div class="kicker">Documents · Data Terms · as published {meta.as_of_date}</div>
      <h1>Data Terms</h1>
      <p class="standfirst">
        What may be done with the published series without asking, and what
        requires written permission.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="sec">
      <h2><span class="n">01</span> Scope and Ownership</h2>
      <p>
        These terms cover the series values, tables, charts, and underlying
        data published on ccir.io (the &ldquo;published data&rdquo;). The
        published data and the compilations they form are &copy; Compute
        Credit Index Research LLC. Photographs and third-party material
        credited on individual pages remain under their stated licenses.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="sec">
      <h2><span class="n">02</span> Viewing, Quotation, and Citation</h2>
      <p>
        The site is free to read. Published values may be quoted and cited
        with attribution to <strong>CCIR (ccir.io)</strong> — including the
        series identifier and publication date where the context allows — in
        research, reporting, internal analysis, and documents. The
        <a href="/documents/methodology">Methodology</a> describes what each
        series measures; a citation relies on that document.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="sec">
      <h2><span class="n">03</span> Systematic Retrieval and Redistribution</h2>
      <p>
        Systematic or bulk retrieval of the published data, redistribution of
        series or series history, commercial repackaging or resale, and use of
        the published data as an input to a derived commercial product each
        require written permission:
        <a href="mailto:research@ccir.io">research@ccir.io</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="sec">
      <h2><span class="n">04</span> Referencing a Series in an Agreement</h2>
      <p>
        Parties considering a reference to a CCIR series in a credit
        agreement, confirmation, or valuation policy should see the
        <a href="/applications#citation-annex">Citation Annex</a> — definitions,
        disruption events, and fallback drafting — and are invited to contact
        the administrator.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="sec">
      <h2><span class="n">05</span> No Warranty</h2>
      <p>
        The published data are provided as is, without warranty of any kind,
        including fitness for a particular purpose. Series are computed and
        corrected under the published
        <a href="/documents/methodology">Methodology</a> and
        <a href="/documents/change-management">Change Management Policy</a>;
        use of the published data is at the user&rsquo;s own risk. Revisions
        to these terms are posted on this page with the publication date
        above.
      </p>
    </section>
  </section>

  <style>
    .top { padding-top: 32px; }
    .page-head { max-width: 80ch; margin-bottom: 10px; }
    .page-head h1 {
      font-family: var(--font-display);
      font-size: var(--fs-hero);
      line-height: var(--lh-display);
      font-weight: var(--weight-display);
      margin: 6px 0 14px;
      letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    }
    .sec { margin: 26px 0; max-width: 76ch; }
    .sec h2 {
      font-family: var(--font-display);
      font-size: var(--fs-xl);
      margin: 0 0 10px;
      display: flex;
      align-items: baseline;
      gap: 12px;
    }
    .sec .n {
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: var(--fs-sm);
      color: var(--accent);
      font-weight: var(--weight-strong);
    }
    .sec p {
      font-family: var(--font-body);
      font-size: var(--fs-md);
      color: var(--ink);
      line-height: 1.65;
      margin: 0 0 12px;
    }
    .sec strong { color: var(--accent); }
  </style>
</Base>
